# torch and the ONNX runtime for a CUDA 12 build.
#
# The index URL is part of the requirement: torch's CUDA builds are not on
# PyPI, and which `+cuXXX` local version you get is decided by which index
# is consulted. `pip-compile` records it in the lock's header, so the lock
# is self-describing and the install step does not have to know.
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu126

-r base.in

# `VIAME_PYTORCH_VERSION` chooses this, and changing it means recompiling
# this lock -- a torch version is not a free variable once the lock exists.
torch==2.12.0
# onnxruntime 1.23.2 ships wheels for cp310 through cp313 only, so resolving
# it under 3.14 fails with "No matching distribution found" -- the
# requires_python metadata says >=3.10 and gives no hint, the ABI tags are
# what run out. 1.24.1 is the first release carrying cp314, and it drops
# cp310, which VIAME still offers. So pin per interpreter rather than moving
# every build onto a new runtime. Upstream f21a0ac1b, as a marker rather
# than a CMake branch.
onnxruntime-gpu==1.23.2 ; python_version < "3.14"
onnxruntime-gpu==1.24.1 ; python_version >= "3.14"
